1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,429
A Seeker tells people you hold crypto. Nest Finance keeps your savings safe,

2
00:00:05,429 --> 00:00:08,500
even if you're forced to unlock your phone.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:14,128
Your protected savings sit in a vault on Solana, and the safety score flags

4
00:00:14,128 --> 00:00:15,254
what's missing.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,715
Moving money in takes one tap, and one approval in your wallet.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,020
Taking it out is different. Before you sign, Nest Intelligence scores the

7
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:34,908
withdrawal and explains it in plain words.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,704
Low risk: it goes to your own wallet. The app computes the score. AI only puts

9
00:00:41,704 --> 00:00:42,908
it into words.

10
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:52,869
Every withdrawal waits a delay you choose, so you or a guardian can cancel it.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,369
Every step is on-chain, and guardians earn SKR each week they check in.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,799
Now, the moment Nest was built for. Someone makes you open the app, and you

13
00:01:06,799 --> 00:01:08,500
enter your backup PIN.

14
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:14,277
It opens an ordinary wallet. Real spending money, real history, and no savings

15
00:01:14,277 --> 00:01:14,869
to find.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,215
Every tab works as you'd expect, so nothing looks out of place.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,962
Meanwhile, the phone's own key has frozen your savings on-chain, and your

18
00:01:25,962 --> 00:01:29,292
emergency contact gets a text with your location.

19
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:36,667
Later, your real PIN shows your savings frozen, and Settings records when the

20
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:38,138
backup PIN was used.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:49,739
This is the guardian's phone. A large withdrawal to a new address is requested,

22
00:01:49,739 --> 00:01:52,500
and the alert already says: high risk.

23
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:59,125
The app scored it 60 out of 100: a new destination, and 91% of the savings. Nest

24
00:01:59,125 --> 00:02:03,100
Intelligence briefs the guardian in plain words.

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,677
One tap cancels it. The money never moved.

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,800
The What-if simulator plays seven attacks against your real setup, and AI says

27
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,138
what to fix first.

28
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:29,869
Here, a stolen key: the app shows each step, and AI walks you through it.

29
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:38,715
You can ask your own what-if, too. AI explains. The program decides.

30
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:43,792
Nest Finance. Savings that can't be rushed.

31
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The same APK on a real Android phone (POCO F6). PINs are set up first.

32
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,500
Phantom signs over Mobile Wallet Adapter.

33
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:53,500
Nest Intelligence explains the withdrawal before it is requested.

34
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:56,000
Backup PIN: a plain wallet opens while the phone's key freezes the savings.

35
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Seconds later, the emergency contact gets the text. Location blurred here.
